    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1147">

                <pb facs="1157" n="871" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg871"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.00/21</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-08-03T16:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 3, 1916, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 3.40 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4654. Your 3608, August 2, 5 p. m. I delivered to Lord Grey to-day your 3606 which reached me this
                    morning. He did not promise an answer but said he would communicate the Senate’s
                    resolution to the Prime Minister and probably lay it before the Cabinet.</p>
                <p>Casement was executed early this morning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
